From 6e85e5a6f324d6803310dc02079624763db837c2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sergey Fedorov <barracuda@macos-powerpc.org>
Date: Tue, 22 Sep 2026 22:48:44 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 5/7] ppc: add AltiVec be_blur

The running horizontal sum of the C version expands to
col_pix[x] = buf[x-1] + 2*buf[x] + buf[x+1] with out-of-row pixels
treated as zero, which vectorizes directly.  Whole vectors are processed
per row with the row masked to zero past width, so the right edge and
the columns beyond it match the C result.
---
 libass/ppc/be_blur_altivec.c | 130 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 130 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 libass/ppc/be_blur_altivec.c

diff --git a/libass/ppc/be_blur_altivec.c b/libass/ppc/be_blur_altivec.c
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..cac0781
--- /dev/null
+++ b/libass/ppc/be_blur_altivec.c
@@ -0,0 +1,130 @@
